      "properties": {
        "project_name": "Mission Bay South Block 18B (UCSF planned)",
        "site": "Mission Bay South",
        "status": "planned",
        "use": "institutional",
        "geometry_type": "approximate",
        "digitized_from": "Real block boundary from real street geometry (src/block_fit.py load_blocks(), trimmed against src/street_geometry.py's fuller street buffer); the plan's own A/B internal split has no mapped street, so it's an equal-area bisection along the block's long axis, not a real line.",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-22: this filename previously held a different record (the UCSF building complex east of the 18A parking lot), REPLACED and RENAMED to 18C after cross-checking UCSF's own June 2025 CAC presentation (map updated December 2024), which identifies that building as UCSF's 'Block 18C' -- an existing Child Development Center, not future institutional space (see mission_bay_block_18c.geojson for that correction). With 18C's real identity established, the 18A parking lot (data/manual/mission_bay_block_18a.geojson, itself merged from the original 18A/18B split on 2026-09-20) was extended east to close the ~1,197 sqm access-lane/driveway gap that used to separate it from 18C, so the combined lot now runs back-to-back with 18C's west edge (convex hull of [merged 18A lot, 18C] minus 18C, minus real streets). That combined ~9,738 sqm shape was re-split into new 18A (west) / 18B (east) via an equal-area bisection perpendicular to its long axis (binary search on the cut line) -- this record is the east half, 4,869 sqm, immediately west of 18C.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "PARTIALLY REAL -- the outer boundary is a real polygonized city block from real street geometry, not hand-traced, except for its east edge (which now runs along 18C's real, already-tracked west edge) and its west edge (the equal-area bisection line shared with 18A, approximate since no real street divides this block into A and B). The extension into the former access-lane gap on this block's east side is an inferred fill (convex hull minus 18C minus streets), not independently confirmed as driveway/parking pavement rather than a walkway.",
        "notes": "No building on this site as of 2026-09-19 (satellite- and building-footprint-confirmed); currently an operating surface parking lot west of the Owens St curve, running back-to-back with the existing Child Development Center building (18C) to its east. The OCII plan's own Dec 2019 Land Use Map designates this block for future UCSF institutional use, consistent with the rest of this campus row, but no specific project, developer, or timeline was found in this pass.",
        "source_doc_urls": [
          "data/manual/_reference/mission_bay_land_use_map_2019.png"
        ]
      },
